Subject: never replace a HIP runtime that is not ROCm with the system copy

AMD's Windows driver also puts ROCm runtime DLLs in the system directory, and the runner's library
path is reordered to prefer whichever amdhip64.dll has the higher file version. That comparison is
right between two copies of ROCm's runtime. It is wrong for a HIP runtime that is not ROCm's: this
one is our own, it talks to our own kernel driver, and a higher-versioned file of the same name in
the system directory is a different product, not a newer copy.

The condition is the one the install path and the compiler flags already use: a runner directory
named rocm_v* is a ROCm build, anything else is not. Every upstream build is unchanged.

Without this change the protection is accidental: our runtime carries no version resource, so the
comparison cannot decide and keeps the bundled file. Adding a version resource to our runtime
later would silently switch the HIP runtime on any machine that also has AMD's driver.
diff --git a/llm/rocm_windows.go b/llm/rocm_windows.go
index 75fb04be..c09520cb 100644
--- a/llm/rocm_windows.go
+++ b/llm/rocm_windows.go
@@ -67,6 +67,15 @@ func adjustWindowsROCmLibraryPaths(paths, gpuLibs []string) []string {
 		return paths
 	}
 
+	// A runner directory that is not one of the rocm_v* ones holds a HIP runtime that is not
+	// ROCm's. Such a runtime talks to its own kernel driver, so a higher-versioned amdhip64.dll
+	// in the system directory is a different product rather than a newer copy of it, and must
+	// never take its place.
+	if !strings.HasPrefix(strings.ToLower(filepath.Base(rocmDir)), "rocm_v") {
+		slog.Debug("keeping the bundled HIP runtime of a runner directory that is not ROCm", "dir", rocmDir)
+		return paths
+	}
+
 	choice, err := windowsROCmRuntimeDLLChoice(gpuLibs)
 	if err != nil {
 		slog.Debug("windows ROCm runtime selection unavailable", "error", err)
